"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KMMPMZJV1S0H2YW\",\"title\":\"Chara Mattampally — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Chara Mattampally\",\"S\",\"Sow & Reap Chara\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"2PVW\",\"Crediting period\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"2PVW\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"14 Sep 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"04 Sep 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://sowandreap.in\",\"t\":\"S | Sow & Reap Chara\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1KJYKEHT01S0WV6M\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-requirements\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KOmLuhU6yzCYYtUWPyQCw4aByEEJ7Q1-/view\",\"t\":\"VVB Policy\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KJYKEHT01S0WV6M/prj_1KMMPMZJV1S0H2YW/pjd_1M2FK17HH1S0BH8W/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KJYKEHT01S0WV6M/prj_1KMMPMZJV1S0H2YW/pjd_1M1P83MS11S028R7/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nChara Mattampally\\nS\\nSow & Reap Chara\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\n2PVW\\nCrediting period\\n01 Sep 2026 to 01 Sep 2036\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nThis Particular project established in the state of Telangana India is processing Cotton stalks which is otherwise burnt openly on fields. The Plant takes 100 tons/day of material as input and produces roughly 25 tons of biochar/day. The syngas byproduct of the process is fed into the precalciner of the cement kiln. The biochar is deployed in the same fields from where the biomass is collected.\\n\\nTelangana\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 13 Sep 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nAudit kick-off\\n\\nA Validation & Verification Body (VVB) officially commences the project validation and verification process. All VVBs are approved and appointed by Isometric based on the requirements outlined in the Isometric Standard and VVB Policy.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n14 Sep 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n04 Sep 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"